   "evidence": "scripts/lint-scope.sh:87 `[ \"$status\" = removed ] && continue` precedes the `$module_re` / unmatched.txt check at lines 88-90, so a removed `.lean` file lands in neither modules.txt nor unmatched.txt; pr-build.yml:849 gates the scope only on `! -s \"$LINT_SCOPE_DIR/unmatched.txt\"`.",
   "file": "scripts/Axioms.lean",
   "fix": "Say \"every changed `.lean` file that still exists is a named module\" and add the deletion step: a deleted module contributes no declarations, and every module that imported it must change (or the build fails), so it is in the seed. The identical wording in the pr-build.yml comment at line 843 needs the same clause.",
   "issue": "The soundness comment claims pr-build.yml scopes the audit only for a build \"whose every changed `.lean` file is a named module\". A deleted `.lean` file is a changed file that is neither listed nor unmatched, so the scope still applies; the chain \"the modules a change can affect are the changed ones and everything downstream\" (line 115) therefore does not cover a deletion from the stated precondition alone. Soundness does hold, but for the separate reason lint-scope.sh:82-86 now gives (any importer of the deleted module must change or the build fails), which this comment omits.",
   "line": "171"
  }
 ],
